# the argument of aquinas-economy-objection.md as claude-opus-5-5 read it: check that it says what the text says
# This passage is the second objection (Obj. 2) to God's existence, which the work later answers.
# No reply is given here, so the objection's own reasoning is written as premises and conclusions.
atom	accounted_other	everything we see in the world can be accounted for by other principles, supposing God did not exist
atom	need_god	there is need to suppose God's existence
atom	natural_reduced	all natural things can be reduced to one principle, which is nature
atom	voluntary_reduced	all voluntary things can be reduced to one principle, which is human reason or will
# S2 is a general principle: what can be accounted for by a few principles is superfluously supposed to come from many.
# Here it is applied to God as the further principle.
P1	S2	accounted_other → ¬need_god	kind conceptual
P2	S4	natural_reduced ∧ voluntary_reduced
# The "For" in S4 relies on everything we see being either natural or voluntary, so nature and will together account for it all.
A1	-	natural_reduced ∧ voluntary_reduced → accounted_other
C1	S3	accounted_other	from P2 A1
C	S5	¬need_god	from C1 P1
